Package: easypaper
Title: Scaffold a Reproducible Quarto Manuscript Project
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Daniel", "Sanchez-Garcia", email = "danielsangarci@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Creates, in one call, the directory structure of a reproducible
    scientific manuscript written in Quarto: sections as separate files, a
    single make.R entry point, journal styles as .csl files, independent
    bibliographies for the supplementary material, figures exported to PNG,
    JPG and TIFF at 600 dpi, and a submission folder holding the blinded
    manuscript together with a data and code compendium ready for a data
    repository. The build logic is copied into the project, not kept in this
    package, so the project stays self-contained and reproducible without it.
URL: https://github.com/danielsangarci/easypaper,
    https://danielsangarci.github.io/easypaper/
BugReports: https://github.com/danielsangarci/easypaper/issues
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1)
Suggests:
    knitr,
    rmarkdown,
    rstudioapi,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    yaml
